WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
- So Jim, you're still doing
standup during these times,

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.180
so how are you making that happen

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.120
and is it better or worse?

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:06.953
- Well,

00:00:08.928 --> 00:00:11.750
you know, I've become so dependent

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.650
on a certain endorphin rush.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.770
I don't know how often
you consistently perform.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:23.440
Obviously this show is a
creative outlet, obviously,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.440
but I did standup 300
nights a year for 30 years,

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.040
and then for four months I didn't.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.980
So there was something about,

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.650
I was craving the
performance, but it's weird.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.280
So I do these drive-in shows,

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.630
where I essentially do

00:00:41.613 --> 00:00:44.690
everyone's safe, social distance,

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.970
a parking car away from each other,

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.560
but you're performing for cars.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.320
So it's a little bit like

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.960
being in that movie, Cars.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.900
Like, I feel like I'm Mater.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.750
Like, I'm on stage

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.660
and I'm the car performing and it's weird

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.660
because the feedback, rather
than applause or laughter

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.130
is flashing lights.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.890
So people will flash their lights.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.140
Occasionally they'll beep.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.537
They'll be like beep-beep,

00:01:13.537 --> 00:01:17.810
kind of like get out of
the way beep is good joke.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:18.643
It's weird.

00:01:18.643 --> 00:01:20.110
It's a different type of language.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:22.110
- Oh that's such a cool
and clever idea, though,

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.710
just to get people one,
out of their house,

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.740
but their safe and all of that.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.720
It's a really great idea,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.736
and I love a drive-in movie theater.

00:01:29.736 --> 00:01:30.569
- [Jim] Yeah!

00:01:30.569 --> 00:01:33.930
- I think they're so
awesome and personal and fun

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:35.453
and kind of a whole experience.

